#
# Conforming fixture for gmeow:InventedWitnessShape — a chase-minted Skolem
# witness carrying exactly ONE gmeow:existentialOrdinal, the documented
# invariant on gmeow:existentialOrdinal's own definition ("Single-valued per
# gmeow:InventedWitness"). gmeow:InventedWitnessShape's sh:maxCount 1 on
# gmeow:existentialOrdinal is satisfied, so validation emits no findings.
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecInventedWitnessSingleOrdinal,
# gmeow:conforms). Lives under tests/ (NOT examples/) so the global
# make validate gate never loads it.
#
# The trailing `gmeow:existentialOrdinal a owl:DatatypeProperty .` triple
# restates a fact already carried by diagnostics/module.ttl (harmless
# duplication) so THIS FILE's own term-reference set names the property, not
# only the class — the docs-coverage fixture-pair dimension credits a term by
# its CURIE appearing as a subject/object NamedNode in the fixture, and
# gmeow:existentialOrdinal is otherwise used only as a PREDICATE below.
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix owl:   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/diagnostics/tests/> .
@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

ex:witnessSingleOrdinal
    a gmeow:InventedWitness ;
    gmeow:existentialOrdinal "0"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger .

gmeow:existentialOrdinal a owl:DatatypeProperty .
